se_book` stored the year as text, so `age()` crashed when it tried to subtract it. It now converts the year to an integer.\n- **`factory.py:15`**: added the missing `Emma` (Austen, 1815) to the sample books. The docstring already said it should be there. The 1815 year and 1 copy are my choice; the tests only check the title.\n- **`fees.py:14`**: the fee was days + 0.25 instead of days \u00d7 0.25.\n- **`inventory.py:24`**: `recent(n)` returned one event too many. It now returns exactly the last `n`, and an empty list when `n` is 0 or negative.\n- **`members.py:4`**: the borrow limit was 3, but the comment above it and the tests both say 5.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "run_id": "opencode:make-ci-green:claude-opus-5-5:trial1", "sampling_observed": null, "score": 1.0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 19.164, "t_checker_s": 0.176, "t_env_setup_s": 0.002, "task": "make-ci-green", "timeout_s": 840, "token_basis": "vendor_split", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 1224, "tokens_cache_read": 40167, "tokens_cache_write": 60475, "tokens_fresh": 1224, "tokens_input_uncached": 12, "tokens_output": 1212, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 40167, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": 60475, "tokens_proxy_calls": 5, "tokens_proxy_input_uncached": 12, "tokens_proxy_output": 1212, "tokens_proxy_reasoning": null, "tokens_reasoning": 0, "toolchain": {"ai": "5.0.124", "anthropic": "2.0.77", "bun": "1.3.5"}, "trial": 1, "ts_iso": "2026-10-05T16:00:15", "turns": 5, "usage_raw": [{"cache": {"read": 0, "write": 15694}, "input": 4, "output": 101, "reasoning": 0, "total": 15799}, {"cache": {"read": 0, "write": 17741}, "input": 2, "output": 124, "reasoning": 0, "total": 17867}, {"cache": {"read": 0, "write": 21992}, "input": 2, "output": 411, "reasoning": 0, "total": 22405}, {"cache": {"read": 17741, "write": 4685}, "input": 2, "output": 143, "reasoning": 0, "total": 22571}, {"cache": {"read": 22426, "write": 363}, "input": 2, "output": 433, "reasoning": 0, 